# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than a bare `text=auto`, which would still hand a Windows checkout CRLF: the
# toolchain is pandoc, gnuplot and xelatex, and a CRLF working copy has already cost us once.
# Python's text I/O reads CRLF and writes LF, so any script that round-trips a file silently
# rewrites every line of it -- which turned a one-wrapper change in `FKS/41/2/1/03/solution.md`
# into a 99-line diff. 51 files were normalised in `Line endings: 51 files go from CRLF to LF`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git neither inspects nor normalises them. Its own detection would almost certainly
# get these right; naming them means it cannot get them wrong.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.ico   binary
*.otf   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.docx  binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.kmz   binary
